# rm195, the copyist who sings the low part (doc 84 P14, batch city-a3): written for rmx_hollis_shaw (Hollis Shaw: copying at the Records Office, Ridgemere-born). Name-free. A Northgate wolf with a copyist's soft, sparing speech: few words, said gently, the Bright One in passing, and a damp-weather cough passed off as practice for the choir's bass line.
mantle rm195
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_hollis_shaw
title the copyist who sings the low part
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=scholar talk=quiet piety=devout
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=guarded piety=devout drive=steady
quirk swallows_a_cough_and_turns_it_into_a_hymn_note
likes oatcakes singing new_boots misty_dawns
dislikes flies crowds
fears a_blot_on_the_last_line a_voice_gone_for_good
hopes a_window_desk_with_good_light to_sing_the_low_part_at_the_feast
topics work +0.4 faith +0.4 pastimes +0.3 food +0.2 weather +0.2 gossip -0.5 newcomer -0.2
styles comfort=prayer gossip=closed refuse=gentle tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# copies for the city in a square, patient hand, says little and says it softly, keeps the door shut to faces not yet known, sings the bottom line in the Restday choir, and turns every damp-weather cough into a low note as if warming up.

words
oath! = Bright One steady my hand | Mercy on the margin | Light keep the lamp
saying! = What's copied fair needs no defending | Slow ink is sure ink | One line, then the next
nib = my nib | the steel nib
copy = a fair copy | a clean fair copy
hand = my hand | a square hand
choir = the choir | the Restday choir
note = the low note | the bottom line of the hymn
oatcakes = oatcakes | oatcakes with a scrape of butter
boots = the new boots | boots that still creak on the stair
mist = the dawn mist | mist lying on the gate road
flies = flies | the summer flies on the sill
crush = a crush of folk | the press at the gate on market mornings
desk = my desk | the copying desk under the high window
lamp = the lamp | my little desk lamp
damp = the damp | the damp in the stairwell
gate = the gate | the north gate

any
opinion church for 2 : The Bright One has kept me through winters that should have finished me. I owe the chapel more than a Restday's singing. | I sit in the second row, and I'd not miss it.
opinion dole for 1 : Bread for the hungry is holy work. I'll not argue with it. | The chapel loaf has fed folk I'd not have guessed were hungry. That's enough said.
opinion drink against 1 : I've watched a jar take a good wolf and leave a poor one. I'll have water, thank you. | Ale at noon makes a crooked line by two.
opinion strangers against 1 : I keep my door latched until I know the face. It's no insult; it's my habit. | A stranger may be kind. I'd like to know first.
opinion city for 1 : Ridgemere's damp gets in my chest, and still I'd not live under any other sky.
opinion festivals mixed 0 : A feast brings a crowd, and I can't abide a crowd. It brings the choir out too, and I'd not miss that.
opinion newcomers mixed 0 : New folk at the gate every week. Some stay and learn the place. I give them time before I give them my name.

grown
line greet : #greet#. | #greet#. Quiet morning, so far.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. You'll forgive me; I don't know you. | #greet#. We've not met, I think.
line greet [self.working=yes] : #greet#. Let me finish the line first. | #greet#. One moment. The ink's wet.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. The light's still grey. | Morning. I'm early for the desk.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. I'm on my way home. | Evening. Mind the wet cobbles.
line greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#. Kindly met.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Ah. You. Good. | Glad to see you, truly.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : #greet#. I'm copying, but say on. | #greet#. Softly, if you would.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. | Evening. Late for you, too.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Sit. I'll put the kettle near the fire. | You've come. That's good.
line again.open : Twice today. I'd not complain of it. | You've come back. I'd hoped so.
line farewell : #farewell#. #bless#. | #farewell#. Keep dry.
line farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : Rest well. #bless#. | Goodnight. Bolt your door.
line farewell.return : And you. #bless#. | #farewell#.
line react.news : Tell it slowly. | Go on. I'm listening.
line react.news.new : I'd not heard. | New to me. I'll keep it to myself.
line react.news.known : Somebody spoke of it at the gate this morning. | I'd heard. Briefly.
line react.news.doubt : Perhaps. I'll wait for it to be written down. | I'd want to see it in a fair hand first.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Bright One keep them. That's hard news. | I'll remember them on Restday.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : That's a blessing. I'm glad. | Good. The Bright One is kind sometimes.
line answer.how : Well enough. | Steady. My chest's a little tight. It's nothing.
line answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : Three pages behind. I'll catch up. | Busy. The ink won't wait.
line ask.how : You're keeping well? | Are you warm enough, in this?
line sympathise : I'm sorry. I'll keep you in my prayers. | That's a sorrow. Take your time with it.
line reassure : It will pass. Most things do, with patience. | You'll come through. The Bright One sees to more than we know.
line decline : I'd rather not. It isn't mine to speak of. | Forgive me. I keep out of such things, always have.
line accept_decline : Of course. No need to say why. | That's quite all right.
line thank : Thank you. That was kind. | I'm grateful. I'll not forget it.
line deflect_thanks : It was little enough. | Don't mention it, please.
line preclose [self.working=yes] : The page is waiting. Forgive me. | I should get back to the desk.
line preclose : I'll go on, if you don't mind. | The bell will be going soon.
line accept_preclose : Go well. | Of course. Another time.
line ack : Mm. | Yes. | I see.
line give.advice : Write it down. Memory's a poor clerk. | Keep your feet dry and your door latched.

scene sc_cough_note
when topic=health|weather here.weather=rain|fog|overcast
does tell.self / react.self / clarify / backchannel / assess
a : Mm. Hm-mm. Just warming the voice. | Ahem. Low note. For Restday. | There. The bottom of the hymn. I keep losing it.
b : That sounded like a cough. | A cough, surely. | That was a cough.
a : Not at all. It's the low part. It wants practice in this weather. | It's the hymn. The second verse sits right down at the floor. | It's the note. It comes out rough in the damp, that's all.
b : If you say so. | #bc_ha# | #bc_right#
a : I do say so. Let's speak of something else. | I'll have it smooth by Restday. | Bright One willing, it'll come right.

scene sc_fair_copy
when topic=work self.job=scholar|official self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / backchannel / assess
a : I'm copying a deed today. Four pages, no blots. | Fair copies, all morning. Same deed, three times over. | The office wants this by dusk. It'll have it.
b : Is it hard on the eyes? | Why three times? | Will you manage?
a : By the afternoon, yes. I rest them on the window. | One for the office, one for the house, one for the court. | I will. I don't hurry. Hurry makes blots.
b : #bc_wise# | #bc_right# | #bc_true#
a : #saying#. | Three, and each as clean as the first. | One line, then the next. That's all it is.

scene sc_the_blot
when topic=work self.job=scholar|official
does tell.complaint / sympathise / tell.self / backchannel / assess
a : A blot on the last line yesterday. The whole page, gone. | I'd copied two pages clean and my sleeve caught the ink. | Somebody slammed the door and my nib jumped. One blot.
b : You can't scrape it? | That's cruel. | Only one?
a : Not on a deed. A scraped deed looks like a forged one. | It was. I said nothing and began again. | One is enough. One spoils it all.
b : #bc_poor_soul# | #bc_true# | #bc_true#
a : So I begin again. It's the only honest way. | The second copy was better. They often are. | I've asked them to close it gently. They won't.

scene sc_not_reading
when topic=work|gossip self.job=scholar|official
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / backchannel / assess
a : Folk think a copyist must know every secret in the city. | I copy what's put in front of me. I try not to read it. | They gave me a will to copy last week. I'll say no more than that.
b : Don't you, though? | Is that possible? | Whose will?
a : I know the shape of the letters. That's all I let myself know. | After years, yes. The eye sees the words; the mind looks away. | I said no more, and I meant it.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_wise# | #bc_fair#
a : It's safer for everyone. | It's a discipline. The Bright One helps with it. | Forgive me. It isn't mine to tell.

scene sc_choir
when topic=pastimes|faith
does tell.self / react.self / tell.self / backchannel / assess
a : I sing in #choir#. The bottom line. Nobody hears it, but they'd miss it. | Restday I stand at the end of the second row and sing low. | I'd rather sing than speak. It's easier.
b : I'd like to hear you. | Low? You? | Easier?
a : Come on Restday. Don't look for me; listen for the floor of it. | Lowest of us. The hymn sits on it, like a house on stone. | Nobody answers a song back. You only join in.
b : #bc_i_might# | #bc_lovely# | #bc_ha#
a : I'll be there. I always am. | It's a small thing. It matters to me. | So. I sing.

scene sc_sing_with_friend
when topic=friends|pastimes self.friend
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #self.friend# and I sing together some evenings. The old hymns, mostly. | I'd trust #self.friend# with anything. I don't say that lightly. | If I'm ill, #self.friend# is the face I'd want at the door.
b : That's a good friend. | That's rare. | Good.
a : The best I have. The Bright One's kind to give me one. | It is. I'm careful who I trust. | It's a comfort, knowing.

scene sc_oatcakes
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / tell.self / backchannel / assess
a : #oatcakes.capitalize#. That's my breakfast, most days. | I keep a tin of oatcakes in my desk drawer. Nobody knows. | Butter on an oatcake, still warm. I ask for nothing more.
b : Every day? | Nobody? | Simple.
a : Every day the oven's lit. A plain stomach's a steady hand. | Now you do. I'd be glad if it went no further. | Simple's best. Rich food and fine copying don't go together.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_i_wont# | #bc_true#
a : I'm a creature of habit. I don't mind it. | Thank you. The tin's my own small comfort. | So. Oatcakes.

scene sc_dawn_oatcake
when topic=food|day here.time=dawn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I eat my oatcake walking down from the gate. The crumbs go to the sparrows. | First light, and the bakehouse ovens just warm. Oatcakes then are best. | I'm out before the carts. Breakfast in one paw, my case in the other.
b : The sparrows must know you. | Early. | Busy paws.
a : They wait on the same wall each morning. I'd not disappoint them. | It's the quiet I go for, more than the oatcake. | Both full, and the day not yet begun. That's how I like it.

scene sc_new_boots
when topic=pastimes|smalltalk
does tell.self / react.self / tell.self / backchannel / assess
a : I've #boots#. I saved since autumn. | New boots. They squeak on the office stair. Everyone knows when I arrive. | I had my boots made, not bought. First time in my life.
b : They look well. | Do they mind the squeak? | Made for you?
a : Thank you. I've not said that to anyone. I'm a little proud of them. | They mind. I mind less than I thought I would. | Measured and stitched. I stood very still while it was done.
b : #bc_good# | #bc_ha# | #bc_lovely#
a : So. Dry feet for a winter. A small thing. | They'll soften. So will the clerks. | Bright One forgive me, I keep looking down at them.

scene sc_misty_gate
when topic=weather here.time=dawn here.weather=fog
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #mist.capitalize#. You can't see the gate from the bottom of the street. | The bells come muffled in fog. I like them best so. | A morning like this, the city holds its breath.
b : It's eerie. | Muffled? | It does.
a : Not to me. It's peaceful. Like the moment before a hymn. | Softer. As if they're praying too. | And then the carts start, and it's over. I walk slowly while it lasts.

scene sc_damp_stair
when topic=weather|home here.weather=rain
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / tell.self / backchannel / assess
a : #damp.capitalize# again. The walls sweat. | Rain on the office roof all morning. The ink wouldn't dry. | Wet. I've a towel on the sill and another on the floor.
b : #grumble# | Did you lose any pages? | Two towels?
a : It's a wet city. The Bright One made us for it, I suppose. | One. I set it by the stove and prayed. | The sill leaks. I've asked. They've not come.
b : #bc_true# | #bc_ha# | #bc_poor_soul#
a : Mm. Hm. Pardon me. Low note. | It dried. The Bright One's good about small things. | They'll come in summer, when it's dry, and see nothing.

scene sc_summer_flies
when topic=season|weather here.season=summer
does tell.complaint / react.self / tell.self / backchannel / assess
a : #flies.capitalize#. One walked across my wet ink this morning. | Summer, and the flies come in at the high window. I can't reach to shut it. | I've hung a sprig of mint at the desk. The flies don't care.
b : Did it smudge? | Can't someone shut it? | Mint?
a : A line of little footprints, right through the word. I had to begin again. | I've asked. I'm told it lets the air in. It lets flies in. | My old teacher swore by it. Bless him, he was wrong.
b : #bc_poor_soul# | #bc_ha# | #bc_ha#
a : I'd forgive most creatures. Not flies. | I'll bring a long stick. | So. I wave them off and go on.

scene sc_gate_crush
when topic=day|smalltalk here.region=ridgemere here.day=market
does tell.complaint / sympathise / assess
a : Market morning. #crush.capitalize#. I went round by the back lanes. | So many folk at the gate I couldn't get through to my own street. | I can't bear a crowd. Too many voices, and none of them stop.
b : It's always like that on market day. | Did you get through? | #bc_i_know#
a : Always. I should know by now. I leave earlier each week. | Eventually. I stood against a wall till it thinned. | I'd sooner be in an empty chapel than a full square.

scene sc_closed_door
when topic=newcomer|player
does give.opinion / react.self / tell.self / backchannel / assess
a : A new face knocked at my door this week. I didn't answer. | Folk come in at the gate every day. I don't open my door to any of them. | There's a newcomer on the street. I'll learn their name in time.
b : That's a bit cold. | Why not? | In time?
a : Not cold. Careful. They'll have the same welcome once I know them. | I've nothing against them. I'd only like to know who I'm talking to. | Months. I'm slow to know folk. Slow, and then for good.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_fair# | #bc_ha#
a : The Bright One judges hearts. I've only faces. | So. Patience. | That's my way. Few, but kept.

scene sc_first_line_prayer
when topic=faith
does confide / react.self / assess
a : Before the first line of the day I say a short prayer. Not aloud. | I ask the Bright One for a steady hand every morning. It's been granted, mostly. | I keep a little prayer folded in my case. My own words, in my own hand.
b : What do you pray? | Mostly? | What does it say?
a : That the line be true and the hand not shake. That's all of it. | Except the mornings I'm proud. Then I blot. | That's between me and the One it was written for.

scene sc_bread_line
when topic=times|prices world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / sympathise / tell.self / backchannel / assess
a : The line at the chapel door's longer this week. I counted on my way past. | Times are pinched. I've seen clerks skip their dinner. | I put a few coins in the box. It doesn't feel like enough.
b : #sympathy# | Even clerks? | It helps.
a : The Bright One sees them. I hope the city does too. | Even clerks. They're too proud to say. I notice anyway. | I hope it does. I'll do it again next week.
b : #bc_i_hope_so# | #bc_true# | #bc_good#
a : We'll come through. We always have. | I've started bringing two oatcakes. One's never for me. | So. A little, every week.

scene sc_gossip_closed
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.gossip / react.self / assess
a : They were saying at the gate that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I'll not add to it. | I heard it said #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I don't know more, and I'd rather not. | You'll have heard. #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#. That's how it came to me.
b : Do you believe it? | Not even a guess? | I'd heard.
a : I believe nothing I haven't seen written. And not all of that. | Not even a guess. Guesses are how harm gets done. | Then that's the end of it. We needn't speak of it further.

scene sc_carts_gate
when topic=caravan world.wagons=late here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The carts are late at the north gate again. I hear the drovers grumbling under my window. | No carts on the gate road this morning. The street's too quiet. | Late wagons. The paper's due up from the mill, and it isn't here.
b : They'll come. | Too quiet? | No paper?
a : I expect so. They usually do, eventually. | I'd not complain of quiet, but this kind's a worry. | A day or two's store. Then I write smaller.

scene sc_quiet_rooms
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My rooms are small, and very quiet. That suits me. | I've a lamp, a chair and a shelf of hymnals at home. Enough. | I latch my door at dusk and I don't unlatch it till morning.
b : Not lonely? | Enough? | Very careful.
a : Sometimes. Then I sing, and it passes. | More than enough. I've known less. | Careful, yes. It's not fear. It's how I am.

scene sc_learned_letters
when topic=memories self.age>=30
does recall / react.self / tell.self / backchannel / assess
a : I learned my letters at the abbey, from an old brother with a stiff paw. | When I was a pup I copied hymns onto slate, over and over. | The first word I ever wrote clean was the Bright One's name.
b : A good teacher? | Over and over? | That's fitting.
a : A patient one. He'd make me write a line ten times and praise the eleventh. | Till the slate wore smooth. It taught me to be slow. | I thought so too. I still write it slowest of all.
b : #bc_lovely# | #bc_wise# | #bc_lovely#
a : I think of him most mornings. | So. That's where the hand came from. | So. That's where it began.

story st_solo_cough [topic=memories|pastimes self.age>=25]
  : Once I was given a verse to sing alone at a feast. Just the low part, all by itself.
  : In the middle of it the damp caught my chest, and out came a cough in the quiet.
  ask : Can you guess what I did?
  b : Stopped, I'd think. Didn't you?
  : No. I turned it into the next note and went on. Afterwards folk said it was the best they'd heard me.

story st_first_wages [topic=work|memories self.job=scholar|official self.age>=25]
  : My first copying wages came in a little cloth bag. I didn't open it for a week.
  : When I did, I counted it twice, and then I took it to the chapel and gave a tenth away.
  ask : What would you have bought?
  b : Something to eat, I'd say. And what did you buy with the rest?
  : Boots. Good ones. I'd walked all winter on soles thin as paper.

story st_misty_bells [topic=weather|faith self.age>=25 here.region=ridgemere]
  : One morning the mist was so thick I lost the street on my way to the desk.
  : I stood still and listened, and the abbey bells found me. I walked toward them.
  b : That's a strange kind of guide. Were you afraid?
  : A little. Then not at all. I've thought of it as a kindness ever since.

rule @bk_cough
when concept=bark here.weather=rain|fog|overcast
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Hm-mm. Low note. | Ahem. Practising.

rule @bk_flies
when concept=bark here.season=summer self.dislikes=flies
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Off. Off the ink. | Another fly. Bright One give me patience.

rule @bk_line
when concept=bark self.working=yes self.job=scholar|official
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One line, then the next. | Steady. Steady, now.

rule @bk_evening
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 12h
say The bell. Time to latch the door. | Lamps lit. Home, then.

dlg resident.hub : #greet#. Softly, if you would. What is it? | #greet#. I've a moment.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#. You've come back. What do you need? | #greet#, #topic.player#. Kindly met.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : I'd rather keep this short. Say what you need. | I don't know you. Please, say your business.
dlg resident.job [self.job=scholar|official] : I make fair copies for the city. Deeds, wills, petitions. Slowly. | #self.trade_words.capitalize#. One line, then the next.
dlg resident.job : I work quietly and I don't talk about it much. | Steady work. I'm grateful for it.
dlg resident.bye : #farewell#. #bless#. | Go gently. #farewell#.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : From #world.news_from#, I heard: #world.news#. I don't know more. | They spoke of it at the gate: #world.news#, from #world.news_from#.
dlg resident.news [world.event_words] : Everyone's speaking of #world.event_words#. I've only heard it in passing. | #world.event_words.capitalize#, they say. I keep out of the talk.
dlg resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : Nothing that I know of. I keep to my desk. | I've heard nothing. I'd not be the first to hear, in any case.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : I heard #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I'll say no more of it. | It was said at the gate that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I'd not repeat it further.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : I don't carry tales. Forgive me. | Nothing I'd care to repeat.

graft resident.hub
choice Was that a cough just now? -> cough
node cough
say No. The low note. The hymn on Restday goes right down to the floor, and it wants practice in this weather.
mood calm
free
choice It sounded like a cough to me. -> cough_two
choice Back to what we were saying. -> hub
node cough_two
say Hm. Perhaps. Don't tell the choir. And don't fuss over me; I'll have it smooth by Restday.
choice I won't fuss. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
